==============================================================================
ONE-LOOP RG SENSITIVITY (simplified example, NOT precision matching)
==============================================================================
M_GUT = 2.0e+16 GeV -> m_t = 173 GeV; SM one-loop, no thresholds.

(a) 120+126: fit at GUT, then run to low scale
        target      GUT fit    low-scale    GUT resid    low resid
          1.60       2.7589       1.6685       0.2981       0.0359
          2.00       2.7615       1.6665       0.1045       0.0762
          2.50       2.7775       1.6792       0.0111       0.1914
          2.76       2.7650       1.6908       0.0000       0.2716
          3.00       3.0000       1.8435       0.0000       0.2654

    Interpretation: one-loop running SHIFTS m_tau/m_b substantially
    (GUT ~2.76 -> low ~1.67-1.69 for these example couplings).  The
    GUT-scale wall therefore does NOT by itself establish a low-energy
    exclusion: running can move the ratio into the observed window.
    This is a SENSITIVITY demonstration, and it weakens any claim that
    the wall is RG-robust.  A definitive verdict needs a full matching.

(b) single-structure M_d proportional to M_e: does running break it?
    GUT   m_tau/m_b = 3.0000   m_e/m_tau = 0.05173
    low   m_tau/m_b = 1.7853   m_e/m_tau = 0.05175
    low-scale ||M_e + 3 M_d||/||M_d|| = 1.2130
    (0 at GUT by construction; nonzero after running shows the exact
     proportionality is NOT preserved by RG.  The low-scale m_tau/m_b
     moves toward ~1.8, so even the single-structure exclusion is
     sensitive to running and thresholds at this indicative level.)

==============================================================================
CAVEAT: one-loop, no thresholds, indicative targets.  This is a
sensitivity example, not a precision low-energy prediction.
==============================================================================
